.TH "GENI\-UPLOADER\-RUN" "1" "October 2026" "geni-uploader 1.0.0" "Geni Uploader Manual"
.SH NAME
geni\-uploader\-run \- upload manifest sources to Geni with journaled, verified writes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B geni\-uploader run
.BI "\-\-manifest " "MANIFEST"
.BI "[\-\-confirm " "CONFIRM]"
.BI "[\-\-log " "LOG]"
.BI "[\-\-state " "STATE]"
.B [\-\-smoke]
.B [\-\-no\-repo\-sync]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Executes the uploads described by the manifest. A write\-ahead journal is fsynced and pushed before every mutation; the acknowledged object ID and each tag result are checkpointed before readback, and every write is verified with a follow\-up GET. An interrupted run resumes from its journal.
.PP
Run this only after a clean plan, and confirm it explicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-token\-file " "TOKEN_FILE"
file outside the repo holding the access token (global, before the command)
.TP
.BI "\-\-manifest " "MANIFEST"
path to the upload manifest file (required)
.TP
.BI "\-\-confirm " "CONFIRM"
pass YES after reviewing the plan; run refuses otherwise
.TP
.BI "\-\-log " "LOG"
diagnostic log file (run default: geni\-upload\-run.log next to the state file; plan default: stdout only)
.TP
.BI "\-\-state " "STATE"
durable state file path (default: geni\-upload\-state.json)
.TP
.B \-\-smoke
upload only the first item, then stop
.TP
.B \-\-no\-repo\-sync
do not commit/push upload\-status.yaml back to the repo
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short summary and the option list, then exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B geni\-uploader run \-\-manifest packages/batch\-01/upload\-manifest.yaml \-\-confirm YES
Upload every pending item in the manifest after a clean plan.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the command completed
.TP
.B 1
failure (see the diagnostic log)
.TP
.B 2
refused (for example a missing \-\-confirm YES)
.TP
.B 3
uncertain items remain; review them on Geni before re\-running
.TP
.B 4
identity or tag verification stopped the run
.TP
.B 5
uploads are verified on Geni; only the repository status push failed
.TP
.B 6
another run holds the state lock
